{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The key compatibility points are fixed-size `fgets` chunks (255 bytes), C-string termination at embedded NULs, 63-byte stored city-name truncation, insertion-order Dijkstra tie breaking, and the original reference-count/delete semantics. I’m implementing those directly over byte vectors so non-UTF-8 input and exact output bytes are preserved; the graph stays index-based and safe internally."}}
